## Remove

```
claude mcp remove {{ serverData.id }} --scope project
```

Then delete `.mcp-servers/{{ serverData.name }}`.

## Install for every project instead

Do this only when the user asks for it. It changes the configuration of the user, and not the
project.

```
claude mcp add {{ serverData.id }} --scope user -- dotnet run <ABSOLUTE_PATH>/{{ serverData.name }} -v q
```

At this scope the path must be absolute, because the working directory is different in each project.
Keep the file in a directory that stays, and do not move it: the configuration holds the path.

## Notes

- Keep `-v q`. Standard output carries the JSON-RPC stream, and without `-v q` the build
  output can reach it and break the protocol. It is two elements, `"-v"` and `"q"`, and not
  one element `"-v q"`.
{%- if serverData.id == "image-utility" %}
- This server keeps every file path inside its working directory, and refuses a path outside
  it. With a project install, that directory is the project.
{%- endif %}
